        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "Wind swept through the open greenhouse door, lifting the notebook’s pages and pushing it farther across the floor whenever Selin stepped toward it.\n\nShe started forward alone, then stopped. Chasing it might only drive it deeper inside. Rain tapped harder outside.\n\nSelin looked at Bora. The words clearly cost her something. “Will you help me recover my notebook?”\n\nBora met her gaze and nodded. “Yes.”\n\nHe moved through the doorway first. When another gust rushed inside, Bora stepped between the open door and the notebook, using his body to shield it from the wind. The fluttering pages settled. Then he advanced slowly from one side, preventing the notebook from skittering away while leaving Selin a clear approach.\n\nSelin saw what he was doing and followed. Bora held his position as she crouched and closed both hands around the same field notebook. He watched her lift it safely from the greenhouse floor.\n\nFor a moment, Selin hugged the notebook against her jacket. Then she faced Bora instead of hurrying away.\n\n“That worked,” she said. “Your help worked. I wouldn’t have caught it so quickly alone.”\n\nBora gave a small, satisfied smile. “Good. We should get back before the rain gets worse.”\n\nThis time Selin did not argue. Keeping the notebook firmly in her hands, she walked beside Bora out of the greenhouse and along the clear side path. Together they returned to the school courtyard as the wind drove the approaching rain after them.",
